-- title:
--   Gluing isomorphisms of invertible modules across a discrete valuation point
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a scheme (in universe $0$), let $t \in \Gamma(X, \mathcal{O}_X)$ be a global section and let $\xi$ be a point of $X$ whose stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,\xi}$ is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, and assume `hmax`: the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,\xi}$ is the ideal generated by the germ of $t$ at $\xi$. Let $L$ and $L'$ be sheaves of modules on $X$, each invertible in the sense of the project predicate `Scheme.Modules.IsInvertible`, namely: for every point $x$ of $X$ there is an open $U \ni x$ such that the pullback of the module along the open immersion $U \hookrightarrow X$ is isomorphic to the unit object (the structure sheaf regarded as a sheaf of modules) on $U$. Assume further that the pullbacks of $L$ and of $L'$ along the open immersion of the basic open set $X_t = X.\mathrm{basicOpen}\, t$ are isomorphic (the hypothesis is the nonemptiness of the type of such isomorphisms). The conclusion is that there exists an open $V \subseteq X$ with $X_t \le V$ and $\xi \in V$ such that the pullbacks of $L$ and $L'$ along $V \hookrightarrow X$ are isomorphic.
--
--   This is the step at which an isomorphism of invertible modules given over the basic open set $X_t$ is extended across the codimension-one point $\xi$ at which $t$ is a uniformiser, the local form of comparing Cartier divisors that differ only along the divisor of $t$. It feeds [`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.IsInvertible.nonempty_iso_of_nonempty_pullback_iso_of_isDiscreteValuationRing`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.IsInvertible.nonempty_iso_of_nonempty_pullback_iso_of_isDiscreteValuationRing), used in the study of line bundles on schemes over a discrete valuation ring.
